{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) X-linked recessive disorder is:", "option1": "Erythroblastosis fetalis", "option2": "Hemophilia", "option3": "Rickets", "option4": "Fragile-X syndrome ", "answer": "2", "exp": "Erythroblastosis fetalis-Hemolytic disease of newborn<br /><br />Rickets, Fragile-X syndrome&mdash;X-linked dominant"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) which is not clinical picture of Erythroblastosis fetalis", "option1": "Anemia", "option2": "Jaundice", "option3": "Cyanosis", "option4": "splenomegaly", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/01_cLNlJ3D.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"888\" height=\"917\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which findings is not match with hemophilia:", "option1": "Bleeding time-Normal", "option2": "Clotting time- prolonged", "option3": "APTT- Normal", "option4": "Platelet count- Normal", "answer": "3", "exp": "Important findings :<br /><br />1. Bleeding time-Normal<br />2. Clotting time- prolonged<br />3. APTT- prolonged<br />4. Prothrombin time- Normal<br />5. Platelet count- Normal"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which proportion of WBC found maximum:", "option1": "Macrophage", "option2": "Monocyte", "option3": "Neutrophil", "option4": "Eosinophil", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/04_oKktmOO.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"898\" height=\"246\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Properties of WBC excludes:", "option1": "Diapedesis", "option2": "Pinocytosis", "option3": "Phagocytosis", "option4": "Chemotaxsis", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/5_GKKZIxK.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"679\" height=\"538\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Fine granules found in:", "option1": "Neutrophil", "option2": "Eosinophil", "option3": "Basophil", "option4": "Monocyte", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/6_wUrg44g.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"601\" height=\"665\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which is horse-shoe shape WBC:", "option1": "Neutrophil", "option2": "Eosinophil", "option3": "Basophil", "option4": "Monocyte", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/7_q6z1bRA.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"728\" height=\"805\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Antibody produced by:", "option1": "T-cell", "option2": "B-cell", "option3": "Macrophage ", "option4": "Neutrophil", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/9_daKgdWd.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"333\" height=\"38\" /><br />1.Phagocytosis<br />2. Antibody formation by B cell<br />3. Immunity by T-cell, B cell,macrophage<br />4. Secretion of heparin by basophil and prevent intravascular blood coagulation&nbsp;<br />5. Antihistamine action by eosinophil<br />6. Eosinophils kill parasites"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Vit-k dependent blood clotting factors exclude:", "option1": "prothrombin", "option2": "Fibrinogen", "option3": "Factor lX", "option4": "Factor X", "answer": "2", "exp": "Vit-k dependent blood clotting factors<br />&nbsp;1. Factor ll(prothrombin)<br />2. Factor Vll<br />3. Factor IX &nbsp;<br />4. Factor X"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Causes of eosinophilia:", "option1": "Prolong use of steroids", "option2": "Malaria", "option3": "Bone marrow disorder", "option4": "Polycythemia vera", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/9_gEl4xRI.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"935\" height=\"1037\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Lifespan of RBCs:", "option1": "90 days", "option2": "120 days", "option3": "4 days", "option4": "10 days", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/11_6y5gJ08.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"721\" height=\"566\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Commonly used anticoagulants in laboratory:", "option1": "2.3% potassium oxalate", "option2": "3.8% sodium citrate", "option3": "Antithrombin III", "option4": "Fibrin", "answer": "2", "exp": "Common anticoagulants used in laboratory :<br />1. 3.8% sodium citrate or oxalate&nbsp;<br />2. Potassium oxalate<br />3. Paul Heller's mixture&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />(1.2 gm ammonium oxalate + 0.8% potassium oxalate+100ml distilled water)&nbsp;<br />4. Heparin<br />5. Warfarin<br />6. Normal saline<br />7. Dicumarol<br />8. EDTA"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Hazards of mismatched blood transfusion:", "option1": "Bradycardia", "option2": "Tachypnoea", "option3": "BP-raised", "option4": "Anemia", "answer": "2", "exp": "Hazards in mismatched blood transfusion / ABO/Rh incompatibility<br />&nbsp;<br />A. Immediate effects:<br />1. Acute hemolytic reaction&nbsp;<br />2. Shivering and restlessness<br />3. Nausea and vomiting&nbsp;<br />4. Chest pain and back pain<br />5. Heart/respiratory rate- increased<br />6. Blood pressure- decreased<br />7. Shock"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Nonmembranous organelle:", "option1": "Peroxisomes", "option2": "Lysosomes", "option3": "Golgi apparatus", "option4": "Ribosomes", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/14_2ADNyOU.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"546\" height=\"381\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which is not correct for composition of cell membrane:", "option1": "Protein 55%", "option2": "Lipid 42%", "option3": "Cholesterol 13%", "option4": "Carbohydrate 10%", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/15_vlTmdZi.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"689\" height=\"366\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Structural integrity of cell membrane provide by:", "option1": "Integral Protein", "option2": "Peripheral protein", "option3": "Lipid", "option4": "Phospholipid", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/16_xvgQin4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"679\" height=\"560\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Lipid layer of cell membrane is impermeable for:", "option1": "Oxygen", "option2": "Carbon di-oxide", "option3": "Alcohol", "option4": "Electrolyte", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/17_zpZTt95.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"821\" height=\"495\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Enzyme found in lysosome:", "option1": "Acyl phosphatase", "option2": "Glucosidase", "option3": "Cathepsins", "option4": "Pyruvate dehydrogenase", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/18_UiUtjpL.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"732\" height=\"544\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Cytoskeleton filaments excludes:", "option1": "Microtubules", "option2": "intermediate filaments", "option3": "Microfilaments", "option4": "Centrioles", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/19_0xVHYpa.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"671\" height=\"314\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Movement of sperm is facilitated by:", "option1": "Microvilli", "option2": "Cillia", "option3": "Flagellum", "option4": "Fructose", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/20_GswKcPN.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"749\" height=\"394\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which type of cell junction found in endothelium of capillary:", "option1": "Tight junction", "option2": "Gap junction", "option3": "Desmosome", "option4": "Hemidesmosome", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/21_0TfKRQI.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"902\" height=\"489\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which one is false about cell organelles?", "option1": "Power house of cell-mitochondria", "option2": "Synthesis of protein-Ribosomes", "option3": "Synthesis of protein-RER", "option4": "Cellular movements-centrosomes", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/22_CAHoFot.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1005\" height=\"785\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Non-chromosomal DNA found in-", "option1": "RNA", "option2": "Nucleus", "option3": "Mitochondria", "option4": "Centrosome", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/23_fmAOyLT.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"558\" height=\"388\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Types of RNA excludes:", "option1": "m RNA", "option2": "r RNA", "option3": "n RNA", "option4": "t RNA", "answer": "3", "exp": "RNA three types<br /><br />Messenger RNA , Ribosomal RNA, Transfer RNA"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Maintenance of a nearly constant condition in the internal environment, called-", "option1": "Homeostasis", "option2": "Homestasis", "option3": "Hemostasis", "option4": "Haemostasis", "answer": "1", "exp": "No explanation added."}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) In case of 70kg adult, Extracellular fluid contains;", "option1": "40% of body weight", "option2": "30% of body weight", "option3": "20% of body weight", "option4": "15% of body weight", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-south